  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "401/oOp4O0RwBIKArKZdsA3Un9w=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:35:49.879Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The upgrade manifest is the declaration that ties a document type's versions together. Its shape, from `packages/shared/document-model/upgrades.ts`:\n\n```ts\nexport type UpgradeManifest<TVersions extends readonly number[]> = {\n  documentType: string;\n  latestVersion: TupleMember<TVersions>;   // e.g. 1 | 2 | 3 for [1, 2, 3]\n  supportedVersions: TVersions;            // the tuple itself, [1, 2, 3]\n  upgrades: {\n    // keys: \"v2\" | \"v3\" | ...  (no \"v1\")\n    [V in Exclude<TupleMember<TVersions>, 1> as `v${V}`]: UpgradeTransition;\n  };\n};\n\nexport type UpgradeTransition = {\n  toVersion: number;\n  upgradeReducer: UpgradeReducer<any, any>;\n  description?: string;\n};\n```\n\nThe `Exclude<..., 1>` in the mapped type is the load-bearing part: **v1 is structurally unrepresentable as an upgrade key**, because there is no version to upgrade from. A manifest is written `upgrades: { v2 }`, then `{ v2, v3 }`, and TypeScript rejects a `v1` entry outright. Each transition names only its *target* (`toVersion`); the source is implied by position in the chain, so multi-step upgrades compose by walking v1\u2192v2\u2192v3 rather than declaring every pair.\n\nOne source behaviour worth internalising alongside this: `normalizeDocumentModelVersion` treats a document stamped `0` or nothing at all as version **1**, not as \"latest\". Documents predating versioning are legacy v1 documents and get the v1 reducer. Resolving them to latest instead would re-pin an old document's whole history onto whichever module happens to be newest \u2014 the exact corruption versioning exists to prevent.\n\nThe generated `upgrades/` folder mirrors this: `versions.ts` exports the tuple and `latestVersion`, one file per transition (`v2.ts`), and `upgrade-manifest.ts` assembles them.\n\n_Source: apps/academy/docs/academy/03-Build/02-DocumentModelCreation/08-DocumentModelVersioning.md, confirmed against packages/shared/document-model/upgrades.ts (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-13T14:35:49.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:35:49.879Z"
    }
  },
